# The LosOS Secure Boot signing certificate: the PUBLIC half of the db key
# that signs the installer medium's UEFI loader (modules/secure-boot.nix,
# losos-sign-iso) and the SHA256SUMS of every release.
#
# Empty on purpose until the owner has run the key ceremony in
# provisioning/secure-boot/README.md on their own machine. The private key
# is never committed and never generated in a session; CI holds a copy as
# the SECURE_BOOT_DB_KEY repository secret and nowhere else. The ceremony
# appends the PEM certificate block (BEGIN CERTIFICATE ... END CERTIFICATE,
# on lines of its own) below this comment; `# ` lines stay comments.
